{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/498470-speculating-on-the-new-integrity-analog","id":498470,"title":"Speculating on the New Integrity Analog","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-01T00:48:41-07:00","id":498470,"title":"Speculating on the New Integrity Analog","content":"In The Obsidian Haberdash-ed One's <a href=\"http://www.blackhatmatt.blogspot.com/2015/04/promethean-lacuna-matata.html\" target=\"_blank\">most recent blogpost about Promethean</a>, there were some new spoilers for 2nd ed. that I thought I should point out!<br /> <br /> First off, it seems the Virtue analog will be your &quot;Elpis&quot;, which as we all know means &quot;hope&quot;. The only example given is of Courage, so not a whole lot to draw on in terms of what sort of ideas you pick for that. But does this mean the Vice equivalent will be something related to the Lillithim or Flux? Nobody knows! <u>Nobody</u>!<br /> <br /> Now as to the title of this post, BlackHatMatt has previously stated that Humanity is no longer the Integrity analog and replaced with something more indicative of your place on the Pilgrimage. I for one think this is a great idea, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">but I'm biased</a> (please excuse the lack of GMC conversion). And what is intrinsically tied to the Pilgrimage, and is constantly rising up and down?<br /> <br /> Vitriol.<br /> <br /> Yup. And I'm betting being on the extreme ends effects things like Disquiet and other intrinsic Promethean Traits.<br /> <br /> <b>Demon</b> plays a bit with Integrity as something you had to risk, and <b>Beast</b> will have it as fuel. Combining experience with Integrity gives me a <b>Dark Souls</b> kind of vibe, as the more you have the bigger a target you become for Pandorans and alchemists, and the only way to keep it is to spend it <i>but then you don't have it!</i><br /> <br /> This is pure speculation on my part, but I'm thinking I've got good odds. And if I'm wrong? Eh, it's just the internet.<br /> <br /> And finally, here's to hoping that whatever BHM was in the hospital for was taken care of quickly, painlessly, and affordably, eh?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","user":"Metamurpho","date":". 05-01-2015, 10:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T02:40:35-07:00","id":498569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Combining experience with Integrity gives me a <b>Dark Souls</b> kind of vibe, as the more you have the bigger a target you become for Pandorans and alchemists, and the only way to keep it is to spend it <i>but then you don't have it!</i> </div> </div> </div>That sounds really awesome... I like the idea of that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T08:38:07-07:00","id":498916,"title":"","content":"I don't know, that doesn't seem quite right for Prometheans. Your place on the Pilgrimage is the measure of your journey to Humanity - falling backward seems like something that should need more of an action, or tragic event, than simply spending a level for something. If it's more like the opposite of Torment - an ability to function, fit in, and hold yourself together - then it's easier to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T12:08:20-07:00","id":499218,"title":"","content":"I know what it is!<br /> <br /> It's [REDACTED]!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T18:03:47-07:00","id":499568,"title":"","content":"I uh...read a certain leaked playtest of a game that mentioned <b>Promethean</b>'s Integrity trait. I wish they'd start up the blog again because I'm much more interested in this game than <b>Beast</b> just because it holds a special place for me, being my WoD intro game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T21:01:09-07:00","id":499730,"title":"","content":"I'm sure it was a magical experience, and I mean that sincerely.<br /> <br /> With that out of the way, don't read leaks people. There are reasons why the developers and writers reveal what they do, when they do, and a lot of it actually directly relates to our personal enjoyment of the innovations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T05:40:06-07:00","id":500210,"title":"","content":"Well, <i>I</i> enjoyed myself.<br /> <br /> Still, to remain on topic, I have to wonder how Refinement Roles would fit into everything. Their goals/rewards seem different than Milestone (which I wonder if they're like breaking points or something now - maybe 'building' points)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T07:44:12-07:00","id":500332,"title":"","content":"I see what you did there.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T09:46:37-07:00","id":548820,"title":"","content":"The Beast Kickstarter preview notes &quot;Pilgrimage&quot; as the Promethean analog, on page 115.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T13:03:48-07:00","id":550588,"title":"","content":"I think I'll probably miss the use of Humanity as something that the Promethean starts with very little of but struggles to increase, kind of like Mummy's Memory (which was clearly inspired by the original Promethean mechanic).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T13:13:25-07:00","id":550594,"title":"","content":"Have we been told that Pilgrimage <i>won't</i> start low and build up? I could easily see that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T19:33:24-07:00","id":551001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/498470-speculating-on-the-new-integrity-analog?p=550588#post550588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'll probably miss the use of Humanity as something that the Promethean starts with very little of but struggles to increase, kind of like Mummy's Memory (which was clearly inspired by the original Promethean mechanic).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026I get the distinct feeling you were exposed to a house rule, seeing as Humanity started at 7 in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T19:33:31-07:00","id":551002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/498470-speculating-on-the-new-integrity-analog?p=550594#post550594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have we been told that Pilgrimage <i>won't</i> start low and build up? I could easily see that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would certainly make more sense to me than starting with high Pilgrimage and slowly losing it. I mean, if we assume the stat represents your character's progress along their Pilgrimage, I would think 10, rather than<br /> 0 would be the natural finish line. I guess it's somewhat arbitrary, but culturally we tend to view higher numbers as being better than low numbers.<br /> <br /> It could very well work similarly to 1e Humanity, just with a different name so that Prometheans and Vampires don't have the same name for their Integrity stat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T03:07:06-07:00","id":551219,"title":"","content":"I would hope it would start low and go high. Something you need to build up, rather than tear down. The Saturnine Night isn't an overlay on a human, but gap to close and an essence to transmute.<br /> <br /> It's interesting to note that a breaking point on Pilgrimage is close enough to the same with Integrity, in that it can grow a Beast's Lair. So it's still tied to concepts like identity and sanity and an ordered mind, insofar as a Promethean can conceive and integrate them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T23:57:25-07:00","id":552621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/498470-speculating-on-the-new-integrity-analog?p=551001#post551001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u2026I get the distinct feeling you were exposed to a house rule, seeing as Humanity started at 7 in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I really hope I'm responsible for that exposure in some way.<br /> Nobody quote that out of context please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T11:57:15-07:00","id":554655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/498470-speculating-on-the-new-integrity-analog?p=551002#post551002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would certainly make more sense to me than starting with high Pilgrimage and slowly losing it. I mean, if we assume the stat represents your character's progress along their Pilgrimage, I would think 10, rather than 0 would be the natural finish line. I guess it's somewhat arbitrary, but culturally we tend to view higher numbers as being better than low numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or the Pilgrimage stat represents &quot;distance from being human&quot;, in which case 0 would be the right finish line. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T19:43:38-07:00","id":555129,"title":"","content":"Generally, in any 2e gameline, the high numbers represent the more human-like aspects in the games, with the low numbers making you more monstrous. The higher your Humanity, the more like a human, and less like a vampire you are. A high Cover cements you more and more in reality as a real person, as opposed to someone wearing a skin. In Werewolf, Harmony may idealize an average of 5, but high numbers still represent as being more human, and low numbers more monster (wolf-spirit in this case). Even in Beast, a high Satiety makes you more human as you rely less on your Lair and Soul/Horror/Atavisms, and more on Nightmares (though you eventually lose all powers at Satiety 10), while at low Satiety you leave behind the subtle psychic powers for the brute force of your Horror-Soul manifesting strongly in Atavism, eventually culminating in a ravaging beast. <br /> <br /> <br /> So, given that thought, I think its safe to say that Pilgrimage will follow the same pattern. They could mess with things, but I don't feel that's going to be one. Starting low and working high feels right. Working high, suffering breaking points that set you back.. the part I'm most curious about, though, is what the new twist on it is going to be. Every game has a twist on the mechanic, and I don't think that just starting low is going to cover it. Humanity ties into all the banes, Harmony idealized 5, Cover can have multiple different instances, and Satiety doubles as the fuel stat. What special thing will Pilgrimage do?<br /> <br /> Pilgrimage measures your journey to the New Dawn. Likely has to do with vitrol and milestones somehow. Maybe the effects of the new disquiet/wasteland, though I suspect that's going to be tied into Azoth, not Pilgrimage. Hmmmm.......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T23:49:10-07:00","id":556633,"title":"","content":"What is the Pilgrimage going to do? I'm guessing it's going to tell you when you've done &quot;enough&quot; to attempt the New Dawn.You start at three or or lower, and once you hit 7 or even higher, you've got enough of a potential accumulated that you're cleared to try. You say your goodbyes, climb to the mountaintop, and call an ArchQashmal a dick (details subject to change). This is where you (might) roll your Azoth, like you did in the old game. If you're lucky, you climb back own the mountain with some frostbite and amnesia, or you take the shortcut and throw yourself off the peak because you can still survive it.<br /> <br /> I have an idea that when you make the roll, you &quot;bet&quot; Pilgrimage and/or Azoth dots. If you blow it, you lose those dots. The Azoth consumes too much fuel, or those Milestones really taught you nothing. Or the scraps of a real soul you had sewn together just burn in the fire.<br /> <br /> There may be other benefits, naturally. Pilgrimage seems like it could be actively ameliorative for Disquiet and Torment. Since Refinements and Transmutations have had some structural changes, it could tie into those, although the latter is traditionally Azothic. Maybe it could be used to hide from Pandorans and Alchemists (fun fact, it's been 6 months since we actually have gotten an open dev preview).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T05:00:24-07:00","id":556754,"title":"","content":"Well, obviously, its going to track your Pilgrimage to the New Dawn. But I was thinking of the other mechanics are tied in. Like how Humanity is intimately tied into virtually all the vampire banes, Harmony reflects how well to step between Hisil and Flesh, etc. Integrity analogs are much more active than they were in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T06:58:45-07:00","id":556857,"title":"","content":"Promethean has always been in an odd place in terms of whether the protagonist is alive or undead. I would rather like it if Pilgrimage factored into that somehow, in a manner similar to the fan-made <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9509-simulacre-an-alternative-morality-stat-for-prometheans\">Simulacre</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-16-2015, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T07:08:03-07:00","id":556859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/498470-speculating-on-the-new-integrity-analog?p=554655#post554655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or the Pilgrimage stat represents &quot;distance from being human&quot;, in which case 0 would be the right finish line. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>When Matt first revealed it was called Pilgrimmage (confirming it to someone who'd guessed right), I asked if that meant it started low and built up, which he said was also a safe assumption.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T08:52:28-07:00","id":556947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/498470-speculating-on-the-new-integrity-analog?p=556857#post556857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Promethean has always been in an odd place in terms of whether the protagonist is alive or undead. I would rather like it if Pilgrimage factored into that somehow, in a manner similar to the fan-made <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9509-simulacre-an-alternative-morality-stat-for-prometheans\">Simulacre</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, I was under the impression it was definitely &quot;differently alive.&quot; There's a vampire book that calls them undead, but I think that's the only one. Everything else has consistently portrayed them as living beings. Book of the Dead and how Awakened magic works are most notable examples. <br /> <br /> At low Pilgrimage, they'll probably be more... construct like (made of wood, marble, or stone, stitched flesh, etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T11:44:57-07:00","id":557139,"title":"","content":"It's hard to speculate exactly how Pilgrimage ties in to Promethean traits, since it hasn't before. Humanity in Vampire still had effects on torpor and social dice pools in 1e, iirc. Harmony was tied to rituals. Promethean Humanity was just straight-up Morality copypasta'd into the Created, and measured how far you got off the path more than how close you stayed.<br /> <br /> I can't say how I feel about an &quot;ever-more-alive&quot; take to the trait. &quot;Less than human&quot; is a tricky space to define without grading it, and that's not taking into account Azoth increasing alongside it. I'm happy with the all-or-nothing approach we've already got, though I'll gladly take improvements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T20:30:57-07:00","id":560282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/498470-speculating-on-the-new-integrity-analog?p=556859#post556859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Matt first revealed it was called Pilgrimmage (confirming it to someone who'd guessed right), I asked if that meant it started low and built up, which he said was also a safe assumption.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. That someone was me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}